<pdd-reason>Testable asynchronous navigation independent of AppKit.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-dependency>core_rust.prompt</pdd-dependency>
Implement src/model.rs with Browser state and a single scan worker.
R1 (MUST): Only successful latest navigation commits current location/history/
visits; a file path opens parent and selects file. Bad paths retain current view.
R2 (MUST): Back/forward/up, refresh preserving selection, directory poll refresh,
sort toggles, favorites and history reset. Refresh MUST NOT inflate visit counts.
R3 (MUST NOT): Display stale results, spawn unbounded workers, alter documents,
or conflate automatic history with manual favorites. Expose errors for UI.
R4 (MUST): Startup restore with Home fallback. Desktop fixtures can inject state.
R5 (MUST): If an externally replaced directory becomes a file, refresh reports
an error and retains the previous view, never showing its parent under an old path.
R6 (MUST): TabbedBrowser manages independent per-tab snapshots of location, items,
selection, navigation history/cursor, status, path draft and pending navigation.
Share one Browser/preferences/worker. Opening/switching/closing tabs preserves
shared settings, never adds visits by itself, invalidates stale replies, resumes
a tab's pending navigation when activated and sorts restored items by that tab's
sort key/direction. Closing the last tab signals the UI to close its window.
R7 (MUST): Save ordered tab folders, independent sort choices and active index
after successful navigation, sorting and tab lifecycle changes. Restore the
session when launched without PATH; an explicit PATH starts one tab. Legacy
settings without tabs restore last folder. Missing saved folders independently
fall back to Home. Reuse one worker and reject stale replies; restoring/switching
tabs does not increment visits. Never persist selection, unfinished path drafts
or runtime navigation history across restarts. Failed navigation retains the
last successfully displayed saved folder.

R8 (MUST): Expose begin_connection() -> u64 and finish_connection(token,
Result<PathBuf,String>) -> bool for platform connection work. Begin invalidates
older scans and suspends polling without saving URL drafts. Finish only accepts
the current generation; success requests ordinary asynchronous navigation,
failure retains listing/history/saved path and shows an error. Any later
navigation or tab transition invalidates the connection token, including a
switch away and back; stale success/failure MUST NOT change the active view.
